  "harness": "local",
  "invariant": {
    "consequence": "__TEXT,__text must take exactly two values across the 2x2, one per depth price, and __TEXT,__cstring exactly two, one per kernel table.",
    "statement": "Two cells that share a depth price must have byte-identical __TEXT,__text. The kernel table cannot change host machine code.",
    "why": "The table arm edits kernels/quantized.h and its generated twin mlx-generated/quantized.cpp. The twin is one function, `const char* quantized()`, that returns a raw string literal, so the table reaches the host binary only as string data in __TEXT,__cstring and reaches the GPU through mlx.metallib. The crown patch is byte-length preserving, ten single-character substitutions per file, so __cstring keeps its size and no address inside the binary moves."
  },
